import ../../../ui/scene_camera.dl

to check scene number {floating-point number:actual} equals {floating-point number:expected}:
    require condition ((the absolute value of (actual - expected)) < 0.0001) reporting "The shared camera projection or picking ray changed."

set origin to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
set eye to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 10.0
set camera to a UI scene camera at eye aimed at origin with angle 90.0 aspect 2.0 near 1.0 far 11.0
set viewport to UI box at 20.0 30.0 sized 400.0 200.0
set projection to the UI scene projection for origin through camera in viewport
require condition (projection's visible) reporting "The camera clipped its target."
check scene number (projection's screen's x) equals 220.0
check scene number (projection's screen's y) equals 130.0
check scene number (projection's depth) equals 0.99
set above to a new vector with x 0.0, y 5.0 and z 0.0
set projection to the UI scene projection for above through camera in viewport
check scene number (projection's screen's y) equals 80.0
set right to a new vector with x 10.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
set projection to the UI scene projection for right through camera in viewport
check scene number (projection's screen's x) equals 320.0
set {near point} to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 9.0
set {far point} to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z -1.0
check scene number ((the UI scene projection for near point through camera in viewport)'s depth) equals 0.0
check scene number ((the UI scene projection for far point through camera in viewport)'s depth) equals 1.0
set behind to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 11.0
require condition (((the UI scene projection for behind through camera in viewport)'s visible) = false) reporting "A label behind the camera remained visible."
set beyond to a new vector with x 30.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
require condition (((the UI scene projection for beyond through camera in viewport)'s visible) = false) reporting "A label outside the viewport remained visible."
set wide to UI box at 20.0 30.0 sized 800.0 200.0
set camera's aspect to 4.0
check scene number ((the UI scene projection for right through camera in wide)'s screen's x) equals 520.0
set camera's aspect to 2.0
set single to a new vector with x (0.0 as a 32 bit floating-point number), y (0.0 as a 32 bit floating-point number) and z (10.0 as a 32 bit floating-point number)
set camera to a UI scene camera at single aimed at origin with angle 90.0 aspect 2.0 near 1.0 far 11.0
set grid to a new vector with x 10, y 0 and z 0
check scene number ((the UI scene projection for grid through camera in viewport)'s screen's x) equals 320.0

# Projection and picking use the same basis and top-left viewport convention.
for each point in [origin, above, right]:
    set projected to the UI scene projection for point through camera in viewport
    set ray to the UI scene ray at (projected's screen) through camera in viewport
    set delta to point - eye
    set cross to the cross product of delta and (ray's direction)
    check scene number (the length of cross) equals 0.0
    check scene number (the length of (ray's direction)) equals 1.0

set side to a new vector with x 10.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
set camera to a UI scene camera at side aimed at origin with angle 90.0 aspect 2.0 near 1.0 far 11.0
set point to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z -10.0
set projection to the UI scene projection for point through camera in viewport
check scene number (projection's screen's x) equals 320.0
set ray to the UI scene ray at (a UI point at 220.0 and 130.0) through camera in viewport
check scene number (the x of (ray's direction)) equals -1.0
check scene number (the z of (ray's direction)) equals 0.0

set eye to a new vector with x 0.0, y 10.0 and z 10.0
set camera to a UI scene camera at eye aimed at origin with angle 35.0 aspect 2.0 near 0.1 far 150.0
set up to a new vector with x 0.3, y 1.0 and z 0.1
set camera's up to up
set view to the UI scene view matrix from eye toward origin with up up
set wrapped to the UI scene view matrix for camera
loop index from 0 to 16:
    check scene number (the item at index in view) equals (the item at index in wrapped)
check scene number (the length of (eye - (a new vector with x 0.0, y 10.0 and z 10.0))) equals 0.0
check scene number (the x of up) equals 0.3
set camera's up to a new vector with x 0.0, y 1.0 and z 0.0
set ray to the UI scene ray at (a UI point at 220.0 and 130.0) through camera in viewport
set hit to the UI scene hit from ray on ground at 0.0
require condition (hit's hit) reporting "The center ray missed the ground."
check scene number (the x of (hit's point)) equals 0.0
check scene number (the y of (hit's point)) equals 0.0
check scene number (the z of (hit's point)) equals 0.0
set ray's direction to a new vector with x 1.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
require condition (((the UI scene hit from ray on ground at 0.0)'s hit) = false) reporting "A parallel ray reported a ground intersection."
set ray's direction to a new vector with x 0.0, y 1.0 and z 0.0
require condition (((the UI scene hit from ray on ground at 0.0)'s hit) = false) reporting "A ray pointing away hit the ground behind it."
set ray's direction to a new vector with x 0.0, y -2.0 and z 0.0
set hit to the UI scene hit from ray on ground at 0.0
check scene number (hit's distance) equals 10.0
print line "Scene cameras share column-major perspective transforms, clipping, viewport projection and normalized ground-picking rays."
